Chapter: TownRoutes
  cites Uoaix chapter TownLivePath
  cites Uoaix chapter GameCombatPackets

 Saved-path stepping follows TownLive's port of Source-X CCharNPCAct.cpp NPC_WalkToPoint, Apache-2.0;
 Sphere-LICENSE.txt.

  RteWalk = record { route : Integer, generation : Integer, step : Integer, x : Integer, y : Integer,
    stalls : Integer, fails : Integer, rest : Integer, blocked : Integer, facing : Integer, moves : Integer,
    sidestep : Integer, detour : Integer, pressed : Integer }
  rte-walk : Integer -> RteWalk
  rte-walk (unused) = RteWalk { route = 0 - 1, generation = 0, step = 0, x = 0, y = 0, stalls = 0, fails = 0, rest = 0, blocked = 0, facing = 4, moves = 0,
    sidestep = 0, detour = 0 - 1, pressed = 0 }
 Eight blocked attempts at one step abandon the shared route and plan from where the walker stands.
  rte-stall-limit : Integer = 8
 After three blocked attempts at one step a walker steps past the mobile in its way: two walkers meeting in a one-tile
 doorway otherwise each wait for the other until both abandon their routes, and the inn's door stayed shut that way.
  rte-pass-stalls : Integer = 3
  rte-key : TlPath, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-key (p) (id) (field) = peek-qword p.route-keys (id * tl-route-key-bytes + field * 8)
  rte-find : TlPath, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-find (p) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) (i) = if i == p.route-count then 0 - 1
    else if rte-key p i 6 > 0 & rte-key p i 0 == m.x & rte-key p i 1 == m.y & rte-key p i 2 == m.z
      & rte-key p i 3 == tx & rte-key p i 4 == ty & rte-key p i 5 == tz then i
    else rte-find p m tx ty tz (i + 1)
  rte-plan : TlPath, WorldTable, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-plan (p) (world) (map) (doors) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) = rte-plan-budget p world map doors m tx ty tz (p.width * p.height)
 UOAIX-216: a failed plan holds a route slot with its count field minus the planner's epoch, and the same start and goal
 are refused without a search until rte-fail-epochs more searches have run on that planner, so a changed door or crowd
 can open the way. A failed plan expands every cell its start reaches; a keeper whose goal no route reached searched all
 117,504 cells of Britain's map at each retry, 9 s guest a slow tick (trial 43354).
  rte-fail-epochs : Integer = 256
  rte-failed : TlPath, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rte-failed (p) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) (i) = if i == p.route-count then False
    else if rte-key p i 6 < 0 & p.epoch + rte-key p i 6 >= 0 & p.epoch + rte-key p i 6 < rte-fail-epochs & rte-key p i 0 == m.x & rte-key p i 1 == m.y & rte-key p i 2 == m.z
      & rte-key p i 3 == tx & rte-key p i 4 == ty & rte-key p i 5 == tz then True
    else rte-failed p m tx ty tz (i + 1)
  rte-plan-budget : TlPath, WorldTable, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-plan-budget (p) (world) (map) (doors) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) (budget) = rte-plan-clip p world map doors m tx ty tz budget False
 A keeper's budget end stores count 0, neither found nor failed, because its RteJob finishes the search in slices. A
 probe has no job, so clip-fails stores its budget end as failed: stored as 0, every tick's candidate scan re-ran the
 probe to its full budget (trial-46829, UOAIX-267).
  rte-plan-clip : TlPath, WorldTable, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  rte-plan-clip (p) (world) (map) (doors) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) (budget) (clip-fails) = let found = rte-find p m tx ty tz 0
    in if found >= 0 then let hit = rte-why p 5 in rte-touch p found
    else if rte-failed p m tx ty tz 0 then let refused = rte-why p 6 in 0 - 1
    else let searched = rte-why p 7
    in let cells0 = p.cells
    in let full = p.route-count == tl-route-limit
    in let evicted = if full then rte-why p 11 else 0
    in let id = if full then rte-victim p 1 0 else p.route-count
    in let at = id * tl-route-key-bytes
    in let generation = (if full then peek-qword p.route-keys (at + 56) else 0) + 1
    in let count = tl-plan-budget p world map doors m tx ty tz (p.route-steps + id * (tl-route-step-bytes p)) (tl-route-step-bytes p) budget
    in let a = poke-qword p.route-keys at m.x
    in let b = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 8) m.y
    in let c = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 16) m.z
    in let d = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 24) tx
    in let e = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 32) ty
    in let f = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 40) tz
    in let g = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 48) (if count > 0 then count else if p.ended == tl-ended-budget & not clip-fails then 0 else 0 - max 1 p.epoch)
    in let h = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 56) generation
    in let used = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 64) hpet-ticks
    in let taken = rte-take p full id
    in let costed = poke-qword p.why 80 (peek-qword p.why 80 + p.cells - cells0)
    in if count <= 0 then 0 - 1 else id
 UOAIX-267: a full table overwrote its slots in turn, so a route still being walked was taken by the next plan anywhere
 in town and its walker planned again at its next step (trial-45907: the gatherer and farmer, timer kind 12, cost about
 one full plan a step). A full table takes the slot used longest ago; a walker's every step marks its route used.
  rte-touch : TlPath, Integer -> Integer
  rte-touch (p) (id) = let used = poke-qword p.route-keys (id * tl-route-key-bytes + 64) hpet-ticks in id
  rte-victim : TlPath, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-victim (p) (i) (best) = if i >= p.route-count then best
    else rte-victim p (i + 1) (if rte-key p i 8 < rte-key p best 8 then i else best)
 A keeper search longer than rte-slice cells runs as the one RteJob, a slice a town step on its own planner (root,
 2026-10-16: a whole-window search in one step stalled the shard about 10 s guest); the keeper waits meanwhile, and a
 found route is adopted into its town's route table, where the keeper's next plan finds it. result: 1 running, 2 found
 and adopted, 3 sealed. A finished job its keeper does not collect within rte-job-keep steps is dropped.
  rte-slice : Integer = 4096
  rte-job-keep : Integer = 600
 The job is built at boot and keeps only boot structures and scalars: the town's door state is bound once (doors) and a
 request says by door-on whether its search uses it, so nothing made during play is stored past a compaction.
  RteJob = record { nav : TlPath, busy : Integer, who : Integer, result : Integer, waited : Integer, town : TlPath, map : WalkMap,
    doors : Maybe WdState, door-on : Integer, self : Integer, start : Integer, goal : Integer, fx : Integer, fy : Integer, fz : Integer, tx : Integer, ty : Integer, tz : Integer }
  rte-job-new : Integer, TlPath, WalkMap, Maybe WdState -> RteJob
  rte-job-new (cells) (town) (map) (doors) = RteJob { nav = tl-path-cap cells, busy = 0, who = 0, result = 0, waited = 0, town = town, map = map,
    doors = doors, door-on = 0, self = 0, start = 0, goal = 0, fx = 0, fy = 0, fz = 0, tx = 0, ty = 0, tz = 0 }
  rte-job-ask : RteJob, Integer, TlPath, WalkMap, Boolean, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rte-job-ask (j) (who) (town) (map) (doored) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) = if j.busy /= 0 then False
    else let start = tl-begin j.nav map m tx ty tz
    in if start < 0 then False
    else let a = __record-set j "busy" 1 in let b = __record-set j "who" who in let c = __record-set j "result" 1 in let d = __record-set j "waited" 0
    in let e = __record-set j "town" town in let f = __record-set j "map" map in let g = __record-set j "door-on" (if doored then 1 else 0)
    in let h = __record-set j "self" m.serial in let i = __record-set j "start" start in let k = __record-set j "goal" (walk-cell map tx ty)
    in let l = __record-set j "fx" m.x in let n = __record-set j "fy" m.y in let o = __record-set j "fz" m.z
    in let q = __record-set j "tx" tx in let r = __record-set j "ty" ty in let s = __record-set j "tz" tz in True
  rte-job-step : RteJob, WorldTable -> Integer
  rte-job-step (j) (world) = rte-job-step-by j world rte-slice
  rte-job-step-by : RteJob, WorldTable, Integer -> Integer
  rte-job-step-by (j) (world) (slice) = if j.busy == 0 then 0
    else if j.result /= 1 then (if j.waited >= rte-job-keep then let freed = __record-set j "busy" 0 in 0 else let w = __record-set j "waited" (j.waited + 1) in 0)
    else let found = tl-resume j.nav world j.map (if j.door-on == 1 then j.doors else None) j.self j.start j.goal slice
    in if found >= 0 then (let id = rte-adopt j.town j.nav found j.start j.fx j.fy j.fz j.tx j.ty j.tz in let r = __record-set j "result" (if id >= 0 then 2 else 3) in 1)
    else if j.nav.ended == tl-ended-sealed then (let r = __record-set j "result" 3 in 1)
    else 1
 The job's answer for keeper who: 0 not its job, 1 still running, 2 found (the route is in the town's table), 3 sealed;
 a finished answer frees the job.
  rte-job-answer : RteJob, Integer -> Integer
  rte-job-answer (j) (who) = if j.busy == 0 | j.who /= who then 0
    else if j.result == 1 then 1
    else let answer = j.result in let freed = __record-set j "busy" 0 in answer
  rte-adopt : TlPath, TlPath, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-adopt (p) (slow) (found) (start) (fx) (fy) (fz) (tx) (ty) (tz) = if slow.width /= p.width | slow.height /= p.height then 0 - 1
    else let full = p.route-count == tl-route-limit
    in let id = if full then rte-victim p 1 0 else p.route-count
    in let at = id * tl-route-key-bytes
    in let generation = (if full then peek-qword p.route-keys (at + 56) else 0) + 1
    in let path = p.route-steps + id * (tl-route-step-bytes p)
    in let zero = wd-zero path 0 (tl-route-step-bytes p)
    in let length = tl-reverse-path slow found start path (tl-route-step-bytes p) 0
    in if length <= 0 then 0 - 1
    else let ordered = tl-flip-path path length 0
    in let a = poke-qword p.route-keys at fx
    in let b = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 8) fy
    in let c = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 16) fz
    in let d = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 24) tx
    in let e = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 32) ty
    in let f = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 40) tz
    in let g = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 48) length
    in let h = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 56) generation
    in let used = poke-qword p.route-keys (at + 64) hpet-ticks
    in let taken = rte-take p full id in id
  rte-take : TlPath, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  rte-take (p) (full) (id) = if full then let a = __record-set p "route-cursor" (int-mod (id + 1) tl-route-limit) in 0
    else let b = __record-set p "route-count" (id + 1) in 0
  rte-drop : RteWalk -> Integer
  rte-drop (w) = let a = __record-set w "route" (0 - 1) in let b = __record-set w "stalls" 0 in let c = __record-set w "detour" (0 - 1) in 0
 A failed plan waits 2, 4 .. 64 steps before the next (F30).
  rte-pace : RteWalk, Integer -> Integer
  rte-pace (w) (id) = if id >= 0 then let a = __record-set w "fails" 0 in let b = __record-set w "rest" 0 in 0
    else let next = min 6 (w.fails + 1)
    in let failed = __record-set w "fails" next
    in let waiting = __record-set w "rest" (bit-shl 1 next) in 0
  rte-queued : RteWalk -> Integer
  rte-queued (w) = let a = __record-set w "rest" 0 in let b = __record-set w "fails" 0 in 0
  rte-unrest : RteWalk -> Integer
  rte-unrest (w) = let a = __record-set w "rest" 0 in 0
  rte-bound : TlPath, RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rte-bound (p) (w) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) = if w.route < 0 | m.x /= w.x | m.y /= w.y then False
    else rte-key p w.route 7 == w.generation & w.step < rte-key p w.route 6
      & rte-key p w.route 3 == tx & rte-key p w.route 4 == ty & rte-key p w.route 5 == tz
 UOAIX-267: why a walker plans again, and what each plan cost, counted on its planner (`p.why`, reset each WHEEL TOTAL):
 0 no route, 1 displaced off its route, 2 route slot reused, 3 route walked to its end, 4 goal changed; 5 table hit,
 6 refused as recently failed, 7 searched, 8 searched for rte-toward; cells searched for rte-toward (9) and by rte-plan (10); 11 a search that took a slot from a full table.
 12 + 2k and 13 + 2k: searches and cells by direct rte-plan site k (0 lumber shun, 1 miner node, 2 gatherer spot,
 3 cgg-plans for cgg-reaches, 4 rock try); 22 probes rte-probe-budget ended; 23 and 24 the serial of the last walker
 replanned for reason 3 and for reason 4 (UOAIX-267: names the walker behind a 3-and-4 loop).
  rte-plan-at : Integer, TlPath, WorldTable, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-plan-at (site) (p) (world) (map) (doors) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) = rte-plan-at-budget site p world map doors m tx ty tz (p.width * p.height)
 A probe that cannot reach expands every cell its start reaches (Britain's map is 127,872); a reaching probe averaged
 about 5k cells (trial-46788).
  rte-probe-budget : Integer = 32768
  rte-plan-at-budget : Integer, TlPath, WorldTable, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-plan-at-budget (site) (p) (world) (map) (doors) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) (budget) = let s0 = peek-qword p.why 56
    in let c0 = p.cells
    in let id = rte-plan-clip p world map doors m tx ty tz budget True
    in let clipped = if id < 0 & peek-qword p.why 56 > s0 & p.ended == tl-ended-budget then rte-why p 22 else 0
    in let a = poke-qword p.why ((12 + site * 2) * 8) (peek-qword p.why ((12 + site * 2) * 8) + peek-qword p.why 56 - s0)
    in let b = poke-qword p.why ((13 + site * 2) * 8) (peek-qword p.why ((13 + site * 2) * 8) + p.cells - c0) in id
  rte-why : TlPath, Integer -> Integer
  rte-why (p) (slot) = poke-qword p.why (slot * 8) (peek-qword p.why (slot * 8) + 1)
  rte-unbound : TlPath, RteWalk, WorldObject -> Integer
  rte-unbound (p) (w) (m) = if w.route < 0 then 0
    else if m.x /= w.x | m.y /= w.y then 1
    else if rte-key p w.route 7 /= w.generation then 2
    else if w.step >= rte-key p w.route 6 then 3
    else 4
  rte-stall : RteWalk -> List (List Integer)
  rte-stall (w) = let stalls = w.stalls + 1
    in let a = __record-set w "blocked" (w.blocked + 1)
    in let b = __record-set w "stalls" stalls
    in let c = if stalls >= rte-stall-limit then rte-drop w else 0 in []
  rte-any : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rte-any (x) (y) = True
  rte-step : TlPath, WorldTable, Maybe GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, (Integer, Integer -> Boolean), RteWalk, WorldObject -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-step (p) (world) (game) (map) (doors) (admit) (w) (m) = let used = rte-touch p w.route
    in if w.detour >= 0 then rte-rejoin world game map doors admit w m
    else let direction = rte-route-step p w w.step
    in let side = if w.sidestep == 0 | w.stalls >= rte-pass-stalls | w.step + 1 >= rte-key p w.route 6 then 0 - 1
      else rte-side world map doors admit m direction (rte-route-step p w (w.step + 1)) 0
    in if side < 0 then rte-try-in world game map doors admit w m direction
    else rte-detour world map w m direction (rte-route-step p w (w.step + 1)) side
  rte-route-step : TlPath, RteWalk, Integer -> Integer
  rte-route-step (p) (w) (i) = peek-byte p.route-steps (w.route * (tl-route-step-bytes p) + i)
 Damian, 2026-10-20: "a guard's path shouldn't be blocked by players or other dynamic blocking items. they should
 navigate around". A walker with sidestep set, whose next route tile holds a mobile that blocks it, steps instead to a
 free tile beside it that touches the route's tile after the blocked one, and rejoins the route there; with no such tile
 it stalls as before. Candidates turn from the route's direction by 1 then by 2, either way.
  rte-turns : List Integer = [1, 7, 2, 6]
  rte-dir : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-dir (dx) (dy) (i) = if i == 8 then 0 - 1 else if walk-dx i == dx & walk-dy i == dy then i else rte-dir dx dy (i + 1)
  rte-side : WorldTable, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, (Integer, Integer -> Boolean), WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rte-side (world) (map) (doors) (admit) (m) (direction) (after) (i) = if i == 0 & not (rte-blocked world map m direction) then 0 - 1
    else if i >= list-length rte-turns then 0 - 1
    else let d = int-mod (direction + list-at rte-turns i) 8
    in let sx = m.x + walk-dx d
    in let sy = m.y + walk-dy d
    in let tx = m.x + walk-dx direction + walk-dx after
    in let ty = m.y + walk-dy direction + walk-dy after
    in let touches = walk-abs (sx - tx) <= 1 & walk-abs (sy - ty) <= 1
    in let free = touches & tl-door doors sx sy m.z < 0 & admit sx sy & tl-probe-in world map doors m.serial m.x m.y m.z d True >= -128
      & (when walk-step map m.x m.y m.z d is Err (_) -> False is Ok (z) -> not (tl-occupied world (world-tile-first world sx sy) m.serial z))
    in if free then d else rte-side world map doors admit m direction after (i + 1)
  rte-blocked : WorldTable, WalkMap, WorldObject, Integer -> Boolean
  rte-blocked (world) (map) (m) (direction) = when walk-step map m.x m.y m.z direction
    is Err (_) -> False
    is Ok (z) -> tl-occupied world (world-tile-first world (m.x + walk-dx direction) (m.y + walk-dy direction)) m.serial z
 The side step counts as the blocked route step; the rejoining step, from the side tile to the route's next tile, counts
 as the step after it. A side tile that is itself the route's next tile skips both at once.
  rte-detour : WorldTable, WalkMap, RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-detour (world) (map) (w) (m) (direction) (after) (side) = let was = w.pressed
    in when walk-step map m.x m.y m.z side
      is Err (e) -> Err e
      is Ok (z) -> let sx = m.x + walk-dx side
        in let sy = m.y + walk-dy side
        in let tx = m.x + walk-dx direction + walk-dx after
        in let ty = m.y + walk-dy direction + walk-dy after
        in when rte-moved world w m sx sy z side []
          is Err (e) -> Err e
          is Ok (packets) -> let pressed = __record-set w "pressed" (if was == 0 then 1 else was)
            in let rejoin = if sx == tx & sy == ty then let skipped = __record-set w "step" (w.step + 1) in 0 - 1 else rte-dir (tx - sx) (ty - sy) 0
            in let set = __record-set w "detour" rejoin in Ok packets
  rte-rejoin : WorldTable, Maybe GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, (Integer, Integer -> Boolean), RteWalk, WorldObject -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-rejoin (world) (game) (map) (doors) (admit) (w) (m) = let direction = w.detour
    in let cleared = __record-set w "detour" (0 - 1)
    in let moves = w.moves
    in when rte-try-in world game map doors admit w m direction
      is Err (e) -> Err e
      is Ok (packets) -> let lost = if w.moves == moves then rte-drop w else 0 in Ok packets
  rte-try : GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-try (game) (map) (doors) (w) (m) (direction) = rte-try-in game.world (Just game) map doors rte-any w m direction
  rte-try-in : WorldTable, Maybe GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, (Integer, Integer -> Boolean), RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-try-in (world) (game) (map) (doors) (admit) (w) (m) (direction) =
    let x = m.x + walk-dx direction
    in let y = m.y + walk-dy direction
    in let crowd = w.stalls >= rte-pass-stalls
    in if tl-probe-in world map doors m.serial m.x m.y m.z direction (not crowd) < -128 then
      let pressed = if not crowd & rte-blocked world map m direction then __record-set w "pressed" (if w.pressed == 0 then 1 else w.pressed) else w
      in Ok (rte-stall w)
    else let row = tl-door doors x y m.z
    in let opened = if row < 0 then Ok (gs-reply [] "") else when doors
      is None -> Ok (gs-reply [] "")
      is Just (state) -> (when game is None -> Ok (gs-reply [] "") is Just (g) -> wd-toggle state g row)
    in when opened
      is Err (e) -> Err e
      is Ok (door-reply) -> when walk-step map m.x m.y m.z direction
        is Err (_) -> let stalled = rte-stall w in Ok door-reply.packets
        is Ok (z) -> if not crowd & tl-occupied world (world-tile-first world x y) m.serial z then
          let stalled = rte-stall w in let pressed = __record-set w "pressed" (if w.pressed == 0 then 1 else w.pressed) in Ok door-reply.packets
        else if not (admit x y) then Err "route step refused"
        else rte-moved world w m x y z direction door-reply.packets
  rte-moved : WorldTable, RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List (List Integer) -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-moved (world) (w) (m) (x) (y) (z) (direction) (packets) =
    let moved = WorldObject { serial = m.serial, kind = 1, x = x, y = y, z = z,
      graphic = m.graphic, hue = m.hue, container = 0, amount = 1, health = m.health }
    in when world-update world moved
      is Err (e) -> Err e
      is Ok (_) -> let a = __record-set w "step" (w.step + 1)
        in let b = __record-set w "x" x
        in let c = __record-set w "y" y
        in let d = __record-set w "stalls" 0
        in let f = __record-set w "facing" direction
        in let n = __record-set w "moves" (w.moves + 1)
        in let eased = __record-set w "pressed" 0
        in let touched = world-touch world
        in Ok (list-push packets (cbp-move moved direction 0 1))
  rte-toward : TlPath, GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-toward (p) (game) (map) (doors) (w) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) = rte-toward-in p game.world (Just game) map doors rte-any w m tx ty tz
  rte-toward-in : TlPath, WorldTable, Maybe GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, (Integer, Integer -> Boolean), RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-toward-in (p) (world) (game) (map) (doors) (admit) (w) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) = rte-toward-budget p world game map doors admit w m tx ty tz (p.width * p.height)
  rte-toward-budget : TlPath, WorldTable, Maybe GameShard, WalkMap, Maybe WdState, (Integer, Integer -> Boolean), RteWalk, WorldObject, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Result (List (List Integer)) Text
  rte-toward-budget (p) (world) (game) (map) (doors) (admit) (w) (m) (tx) (ty) (tz) (budget) =
    if rte-bound p w m tx ty tz then rte-step p world game map doors admit w m
    else let reason = rte-unbound p w m
    in let dropped = rte-drop w
    in if w.rest > 0 then let waited = __record-set w "rest" (w.rest - 1) in Ok []
    else let counted = rte-why p reason
    in let named = if reason == 3 | reason == 4 then poke-qword p.why ((20 + reason) * 8) m.serial else 0
    in let before = peek-qword p.why 56
    in let cells0 = p.cells
    in let id = rte-plan-budget p world map doors m tx ty tz budget
    in let toward = if peek-qword p.why 56 > before then rte-why p 8 else 0
    in let costed = poke-qword p.why 72 (peek-qword p.why 72 + p.cells - cells0)
    in let paced = rte-pace w id
    in if id < 0 then Ok []
    else let a = __record-set w "route" id
    in let b = __record-set w "generation" (rte-key p id 7)
    in let c = __record-set w "step" 0
    in let d = __record-set w "x" m.x
    in let e = __record-set w "y" m.y
    in rte-step p world game map doors admit w m
